quran[14]{c,v,t}:
  18,84,We had established his power in the land and granted him the resources to achieve everything (necessary for his role).
  18,85,"So he travelled on a particular route,"
  18,86,"until he reached the place (towards the west) where he perceived the sun setting. He found it (seemingly) setting into a spring of murky hot water.* And he found some people (living) nearby. We said: ‘O Dhu al-Qarnayn, you may either punish them or treat them kindly.’"
  18,87,"He said: ‘As for him who does wrong, we shall punish him. Then he shall be returned to his Lord. And He will punish him with a dreadful torment."
  18,88,"But as for the one who believes and acts righteously, he shall have a beautiful reward. And We shall speak to him a gentle word of our command.’"
  18,89,"Then (after consolidating his conquests in the west) he travelled on another route,"
  18,90,until he reached the place (towards the east) where he perceived (the rising of) the sun. He found it (seemingly) rising over a people for whom We had not made any shelter from it.
  18,91,"So it was. And We comprehended whatever he possessed in (Our) knowledge,"
  18,92,"then he followed another route,"
  18,93,until he reached (a place) between two barriers. He found beside them a people who could hardly understand a word.
  18,94,"They said: ‘O Dhu al-Qarnayn! Indeed, Gog and Magog are making trouble in the land. Should we pay you a tribute, provided you build a barrier between them and us?’"
  18,95,"He said: ‘Whatever my Lord has established me with is better (than what you are offering). So, help me with some workforce. I will put up a fortified barricade between you and them."
  18,96,"Bring me blocks of iron.’ Then, when he had levelled up the space between the two top sides, he said: ‘Blow!’ When he had turned it into fire, he said: ‘Bring me some molten copper to pour over it.’"
  18,97,So they (Gog and Magog) could neither cross over it nor make a tunnel through it.
